{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensing from action. The specification binds obstacle sensor outcomes to safe, coverage-oriented actions, ensuring conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration. Exploration alternates between random_walk and short forward moves, with obstacle recovery via directed turns or, as a last resort, a full scan. All obstacle events force a turn recovery before resuming exploration.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to cleanly model uncontrollable sensor outcomes and controllable actions.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward in commit, directed turn recovery on obstacles, and full_rotate only as a last-resort escape."
  ],
